   "the neverending project to convert famitempxpreshystem-users to daydream"


                      [«· Chatfool by Joo/Toytools ·»]

                       Fakechat door for DayDream BBS

                          Version 1.0  [11-May-97]


  Introduction
  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
  Chatfool is a SysOp chat-emulator, fake-chat, shitshat or whatever,
  you name it. It's a useless crapware door but can be worth some wicked
  laughs. The main inspiration for doing this kind of junk were the local
  PC-idiots who kept on paging with reasons like "where are all pc-files?"
  and "i want ware" etc. This kind of door is ideal when you are on a long
  holiday, in army etc. Now you are available 24 hours all day long! :)

  Requirements
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Requires a running (Amiga) DayDream BBS and dreamdoor.library v5.

  File Installation
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Copy the directories and files to your "DayDream:" assign.

  Door Installation
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Install as normal DayDream BBS door.

DOOR_COMMAND.. O
DOOR_TYPE..... 1
DOOR_SECURITY. 5
DOOR_EXECUTE.. Doors:Chatfool %N
DOOR_CONFS1... XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
DOOR_CONFS2... XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

  Environment-Variable
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Chatfool optionally has a environmental variable called "Chatfool".
  You set this variable with the SetENV dos-command.

     SetENV Chatfool [accesslevel]

     eg. 

     SetENV Chatfool 220

  This variable tells Chatfool if to use real paging or chatfool.
  If user's accesslevel is higher than the variable's, real paging is used.
  If it's lower, Chatfool is started!

  Note! If "Chatfool" variable doesn't exist, Chatfool checks if SysOp
  is available. If he is, normal paging will be used. If he isn't, Chatfool
  will be started!

  Configuration
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Configuration file must be in your DayDream config directory.
  Own config files can be used for different nodes, displaymodes, access
  levels etc. You can even tailor own configs for certain users!

  Configuration filename formats:

    ToyJoin.usrX.CFG
               |
               `--- User slot

    ToyJoin.nX.dmY.axZ.CFG
            |   |   |
            |   |   `--- Access level (001-255)
            |   `--- Display mode (1-254)
            `--- Node (1-254)

  Some examples:

     Chatfool.n1.dm3.ax210.CFG   (node 1, displaymode 3, access 210)
     Chatfool.n4.dm1.CFG         (node 4, displaymode 1)
     Chatfool.ax050.CFG          (access 50)
     Chatfool.usr62.CFG          (user 62)
     Chatfool.CFG                (normal configuration)

  If there are no special configs for the user, the normal "Chatfool.CFG"
  will be loaded.

--- clip --------------------------------------------------------------------

PERSONALITIES.. 2
*
PERSONALITY.... Hullu-Formula-SysOp
STRINGS_FILE... Daydream:Configs/Chatfool/Chatfool.1
RANDOM_MODE.... 4
TYPING_SPEED... 3
TYPING_VARIETY. 6
ERROR_PERCENT.. 3
ERROR_CORRECT.. 90
PAUSE_SECONDS.. 2
PAUSE_VARIETY.. 3
IDLE_COUNT..... 1
LOGFILE........ Daydream:Logfiles/Chatfool.log
+
PERSONALITY.... Vaihto-Oppilas
STRINGS_FILE... Daydream:Configs/Chatfool/Chatfool.2
RANDOM_MODE.... -
TYPING_SPEED... 4
TYPING_VARIETY. 6
ERROR_PERCENT.. 3
ERROR_CORRECT.. 75
PAUSE_SECONDS.. 3
PAUSE_VARIETY.. 3
IDLE_COUNT..... 3
LOGFILE........ Daydream:Logfiles/Chatfool.log
+
preset 3
+
preset 4 etc.
~
--- clip --------------------------------------------------------------------

PERSONALITIES.. <number>

	;this is the number of "presets" after the "*" character
	;note that the number of presets is unlimited, just add new
	;ones and put "+" as separator and "~" as endmark.

PERSONALITY.... <string>

	;this is just a "personality description" of the preset

STRINGS_FILE... <filename>

	;full path and filename for the strings file (see below)

RANDOM_MODE.... <number or ->

	;number of strings to randomly show from the strings file or "-"
	;that means that all strings from the main strings will be shown

TYPING_SPEED... <number>

	;basic typing speed in ticks (50 per second)

TYPING_VARIETY. <number>

	;typing speed variety in ticks, will be randomized and added to
	;the basic speed

ERROR_PERCENT.. <number>

	;percentual typo making probability

ERROR_CORRECT.. <number>

	;when typo happens, percentual probability to fix it

PAUSE_SECONDS.. <number>

	;how many seconds to wait for the user's sentence

PAUSE_VARIETY.. <number>

	;pause variety in seconds, will be added to the basic value

IDLE_COUNT..... <number>

	;wait n silent sentences (users types less than 4 characters) before
	;displaying a silence string (see below)

LOGFILE........ <filename>

	;full path and filename where to store the chats

  Strings
  ~~~~~~~
  Strings files tell Chatfool what to write. Here's an example.

--- clip --------------------------------------------------------------------

===[ starting strings ]===
hi %h!.. what's up..ÿd need better access?? :)
===[ main strings ]===
well m8.. ÿd.. i'm sure heard about you, ÿdthough don't remember where ..
ah, give it a fucking break will ya!!
you?ÿd whatta.. ÿd
huh, yeah right!!
===[ silence strings ]===
you got nothing to say for defense.. .ÿdor do you?
===[ ending strings ]===
don't come back here. .you idiot!

--- clip --------------------------------------------------------------------

===[ starting strings ]===	the chat start string
				randomly chosen if there's more than one
  
===[ main strings ]===		main strings
				if RANDOM_MODE is "-", all will be shown
				but if you put a number to RANDOM_MODE,
				that much strings will be randomly picked

===[ silence strings ]===	when user doesn't write more than 3 characters
				for n (see IDLE_COUNT) sentences, this
				string will be shown
				randomly chosen if there's more than one

===[ ending strings ]===	the chat end string
				randomly chosen if there's more than one

  %h	handle lowercase
  %H    handle normal
  %l    location lowercase
  %L    location normal

  ÿd    short delay
  ÿD    a little longer delay

  Other info
  ~~~~~~~~~~
  Ctrl-C can be used to quit Chatfool but only when it's users "turn"
  to write. When computer writes, users can't intervene the writing.
  Well, after all, this is just a fakechat door. :)

  When the chat starts, "Chatfool_On" is displayed. And when chat ends,
  "Chatfool_Off" is displayed.

